1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:05,086
Soaring over high mountains and deep valleys

2
00:00:05,447 --> 00:00:08,653
A ninja's body like an airplane, flying freely in the sky

3
00:00:08,905 --> 00:00:12,338
Honest and kind, Hattori-kun brings joy to everyone

4
00:00:12,492 --> 00:00:15,672
Eyes wide and round, mouth tightly shut

5
00:00:16,005 --> 00:00:19,406
Hiding his face behind a mask, puffing up his cheeks

6
00:00:19,572 --> 00:00:22,730
Catching villains with agile moves, fast as lightning

7
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:26,497
Catching bad guys with quirky new tricks, just like magic

8
00:00:26,850 --> 00:00:29,876
Speaking like poetry, polite and spirited

9
00:00:32,022 --> 00:00:34,848
"Dad's Weight-Loss Strategy"

10
00:00:44,361 --> 00:00:46,558
Dad, we're almost at our stop

11
00:00:46,598 --> 00:00:48,572
Hurry and get our things down from above

12
00:00:48,808 --> 00:00:50,043
Okay...

13
00:00:50,083 --> 00:00:50,906
Ouch!

14
00:00:51,316 --> 00:00:52,823
Oh dear...

15
00:01:05,512 --> 00:01:07,024
And that's that

16
00:01:07,156 --> 00:01:08,410
Were you out shopping?

17
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:10,623
Yes... just a few things

18
00:01:12,343 --> 00:01:14,402
Nice weather today, isn't it?

19
00:01:16,046 --> 00:01:17,676
We really did go shopping earlier

20
00:01:17,716 --> 00:01:20,117
Dad's pants didn't rip or split at the seams!

21
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:25,884
That was so embarrassing!

22
00:01:32,764 --> 00:01:33,497
Mom

23
00:01:33,643 --> 00:01:34,877
This dressing gown is too tight

24
00:01:34,923 --> 00:01:36,408
It doesn't even cover my belly

25
00:01:36,449 --> 00:01:39,716
That's not the gown's fault, you're just getting fatter

26
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:40,903
Yeah

27
00:01:46,837 --> 00:01:48,353
You're too fat

28
00:01:48,393 --> 00:01:49,723
Dad really is too fat

29
00:01:49,770 --> 00:01:52,189
I really don't want to be embarrassed in front of the neighbours anymore

30
00:01:52,338 --> 00:01:53,157
Hattori-kun

31
00:01:53,198 --> 00:01:55,563
Do you have a way to help Dad lose weight?

32
00:01:55,603 --> 00:01:57,194
Actually, helping Dad lose weight...

33
00:01:57,235 --> 00:01:58,981
...isn't very hard, yan...

34
00:02:00,194 --> 00:02:03,621
One, two, three, four...

35
00:02:03,662 --> 00:02:05,506
Now, work hard on your exercises

36
00:02:05,546 --> 00:02:06,425
All right

37
00:02:06,598 --> 00:02:07,324
Let's begin!

38
00:02:07,365 --> 00:02:13,208
-One, two...
-One, two...

39
00:02:13,481 --> 00:02:16,761
-One, two...
-One, two...

40
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:21,626
Ouch, ow...

41
00:02:23,914 --> 00:02:26,060
One, two...

42
00:02:26,101 --> 00:02:28,594
-Ow...
-Dad, you're back from your run!

43
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,484
Finally made it back

44
00:02:34,205 --> 00:02:36,067
Mom, get me another glass of water

45
00:02:36,108 --> 00:02:37,068
Coming up

46
00:02:43,113 --> 00:02:43,845
Ouch!

47
00:02:43,885 --> 00:02:45,964
Dad, what's wrong?

48
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:55,622
Dad, if you want to lose weight...

49
00:02:55,663 --> 00:02:57,364
...fasting is the best way

50
00:02:57,404 --> 00:02:58,405
Fasting?

51
00:02:58,445 --> 00:03:00,205
If you don't eat anything for ten days...

52
00:03:00,245 --> 00:03:02,318
...you'll definitely slim down in no time

53
00:03:05,526 --> 00:03:07,478
-Time to eat!
-Time to eat!

54
00:03:09,568 --> 00:03:11,168
Wow, this is delicious!

55
00:03:14,864 --> 00:03:16,214
Ugh...

56
00:03:19,636 --> 00:03:21,839
Dad, you have to hang in there!

57
00:03:21,879 --> 00:03:23,092
Over these ten days...

58
00:03:23,132 --> 00:03:24,893
...I'll fast along with you

59
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:27,059
Hattori-kun, thank you!

60
00:03:35,485 --> 00:03:36,518
Move here

61
00:03:37,349 --> 00:03:38,588
Are you making this move?

62
00:03:38,629 --> 00:03:40,263
Then I'll play...

63
00:03:40,719 --> 00:03:41,675
That's right

64
00:03:43,698 --> 00:03:45,375
It's a rice ball!

65
00:03:48,663 --> 00:03:51,022
Dad, why are you eating a game piece?

66
00:03:51,653 --> 00:03:54,332
I haven't eaten a thing in four days

67
00:03:54,372 --> 00:03:57,495
So I'm starving, and it looked like a rice ball

68
00:04:11,317 --> 00:04:12,367
Welcome!

69
00:04:12,806 --> 00:04:15,052
Shishimaru, Dad's going into a restaurant to eat!

70
00:04:15,094 --> 00:04:16,693
You can't go in there...

71
00:04:21,603 --> 00:04:23,598
Awesome, it's a steamed bun!

72
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:27,559
Ouch, that hurts...

73
00:04:27,599 --> 00:04:29,105
Ouch...

74
00:04:32,255 --> 00:04:34,937
Unbelievable, Dad is acting really strange

75
00:04:34,977 --> 00:04:36,729
A person biting a dog? Now I've seen everything!

76
00:04:36,829 --> 00:04:38,175
I'm so sorry

77
00:04:39,942 --> 00:04:41,649
Ah, what's wrong with Dad?

78
00:04:41,783 --> 00:04:44,163
I see an apple and a steamed bun!

79
00:04:44,316 --> 00:04:45,908
No... I'm not an apple!

80
00:04:45,949 --> 00:04:47,190
I'm Shinzo!

81
00:04:47,230 --> 00:04:49,550
- An apple!
- Shinzo, what's going on?

82
00:04:52,501 --> 00:04:54,871
Ah, I see a steamed bun!

83
00:04:54,911 --> 00:04:56,393
Ah, Dad, what are you doing?

84
00:04:56,433 --> 00:04:57,347
Ouch...

85
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,236
Wait, don't run away!

86
00:04:59,737 --> 00:05:00,907
Rice ball, steamed bun...

87
00:05:00,948 --> 00:05:02,750
I'm not an apple, help!

88
00:05:02,791 --> 00:05:05,157
- Don't run...
- Help, don't eat me!

89
00:05:05,198 --> 00:05:06,590
Don't run away!

90
00:05:06,631 --> 00:05:09,127
Ah, Dad's trying to eat us!

91
00:05:09,728 --> 00:05:11,089
Dad, what's going on?

92
00:05:14,092 --> 00:05:16,134
This is great, there's cake to eat!

93
00:05:16,175 --> 00:05:18,435
And rice balls, steamed buns...

94
00:05:18,538 --> 00:05:19,445
And apples too!

95
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:20,661
Ah, I love this!

96
00:05:20,701 --> 00:05:22,941
I'm going to gobble it all up!

97
00:05:22,982 --> 00:05:24,575
Ah, Hattori-kun!

98
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,626
Why did you call me?

99
00:05:30,733 --> 00:05:33,773
Ah, there's even chicken skewers!

100
00:05:38,375 --> 00:05:41,187
Dad, pull yourself together, don't be like this!

101
00:05:42,742 --> 00:05:43,697
I...

102
00:05:43,783 --> 00:05:46,297
What on earth am I doing?

103
00:05:46,548 --> 00:05:48,983
But I'm so hungry

104
00:05:49,024 --> 00:05:50,464
Fasting was a good idea at first

105
00:05:50,504 --> 00:05:53,064
Unfortunately it dragged everyone in, so we have to stop

106
00:05:53,344 --> 00:05:55,104
- Really? We can eat?
- That's right

107
00:05:55,144 --> 00:05:57,857
But you can't eat as much as you used to

108
00:05:58,110 --> 00:06:00,130
Yes... understood...

109
00:06:03,451 --> 00:06:04,894
Can we eat now?

110
00:06:06,251 --> 00:06:09,089
Time to eat... So tasty... Delicious...

111
00:06:12,842 --> 00:06:15,332
I haven't eaten anything in five days!

112
00:06:21,566 --> 00:06:22,940
If Dad keeps eating like this

113
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:25,767
it'll all be for nothing, yan...

114
00:06:28,242 --> 00:06:30,963
"Hide-and-Seek on the Train"

115
00:06:36,475 --> 00:06:39,155
Mom, I want to go to Kyoto with you guys too!

116
00:06:39,195 --> 00:06:40,355
You can't come

117
00:06:40,395 --> 00:06:42,394
Dad and I have urgent business there

118
00:06:42,434 --> 00:06:43,863
We'll be back tonight

119
00:06:43,904 --> 00:06:45,354
Besides, the train is quite expensive

120
00:06:45,394 --> 00:06:46,434
So you'd better not go

121
00:06:46,475 --> 00:06:47,140
Oh dear

122
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:47,991
Mom

123
00:06:48,114 --> 00:06:50,320
You don't need to explain so much to Kenichi

124
00:06:50,361 --> 00:06:51,393
Oh, Dad!

125
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:54,065
Bottom line is, he should just watch the house properly

126
00:06:54,106 --> 00:06:54,901
Let's go

127
00:06:55,034 --> 00:06:56,035
I'm so jealous

128
00:06:56,075 --> 00:06:57,917
It's still a long time before the train departs

129
00:06:57,957 --> 00:07:00,036
Why don't we go on the train and take a look around?

130
00:07:00,239 --> 00:07:01,519
Sounds good, come on

131
00:07:02,443 --> 00:07:03,930
-Oops!
-Oops!

132
00:07:03,970 --> 00:07:05,451
Look, a three-hour train ride

133
00:07:05,491 --> 00:07:06,931
will get you right to Kyoto

134
00:07:06,971 --> 00:07:08,252
What? That fast?

135
00:07:08,292 --> 00:07:10,732
Even a master ninja couldn't do that

136
00:07:10,778 --> 00:07:12,899
Look, here's the restroom

137
00:07:13,813 --> 00:07:16,631
Kenichi, your face is so dirty

138
00:07:17,574 --> 00:07:19,852
Let me wash my face first

139
00:07:24,237 --> 00:07:25,621
This is the dining car

140
00:07:25,661 --> 00:07:27,231
It's so nice!

141
00:07:27,341 --> 00:07:29,610
I can even smell curry

142
00:07:30,030 --> 00:07:31,563
I'm hungry

143
00:07:31,657 --> 00:07:33,457
Big Brother, wait!

144
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:35,020
It's not time yet

145
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:36,327
No

146
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:37,740
I need to pee

147
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:39,140
-Oops!
-Oops!

148
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:42,274
I can't hold it... it's an emergency!

149
00:07:43,283 --> 00:07:45,213
Here, go on, go!

150
00:07:46,727 --> 00:07:47,929
Attention, passengers

151
00:07:47,969 --> 00:07:50,492
The train bound for Kyoto will be departing shortly

152
00:07:50,532 --> 00:07:53,025
-All visitors seeing off passengers, please leave the train
-Shinzo, hurry up!

153
00:07:53,059 --> 00:07:54,165
Not done yet!

154
00:07:54,457 --> 00:07:56,820
Oh no, we're in trouble now!

155
00:08:05,573 --> 00:08:07,044
What are we going to do now?

156
00:08:07,085 --> 00:08:08,299
All done

157
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:10,082
Feels so much better now

158
00:08:10,122 --> 00:08:12,504
Shinzo, you've really doomed us this time!

159
00:08:12,545 --> 00:08:13,764
The train has already started moving

160
00:08:13,804 --> 00:08:15,585
Kenichi, isn't this great?

161
00:08:15,626 --> 00:08:17,327
We can take this opportunity

162
00:08:17,367 --> 00:08:18,842
to go sightseeing in Kyoto

163
00:08:19,048 --> 00:08:20,650
Kenichi, I heard you say

164
00:08:20,690 --> 00:08:22,371
you really wanted to visit Kyoto, right?

165
00:08:22,411 --> 00:08:24,942
But riding the train without a ticket is illegal

166
00:08:25,212 --> 00:08:27,093
Have your tickets ready, ticket inspection now!

167
00:08:27,133 --> 00:08:29,463
Oh no, hide...

168
00:08:35,722 --> 00:08:37,371
Hey, show me your ticket

169
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:38,976
Help!

170
00:08:39,016 --> 00:08:41,577
You jerk! If you bully Kenichi, I won't let you get away with it!

171
00:08:43,457 --> 00:08:45,537
What's going on? Hey... don't kill me!

172
00:08:45,577 --> 00:08:46,670
Please don't...

173
00:08:48,403 --> 00:08:49,876
Kenichi, I have money!

174
00:08:49,917 --> 00:08:51,103
Here, take it

175
00:08:53,467 --> 00:08:56,007
I want to buy a ticket, please give me one

176
00:08:56,531 --> 00:08:58,173
I'm riding without a ticket too!

177
00:09:00,936 --> 00:09:03,970
Hattori-kun, I really didn't expect you to have money

178
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:05,217
We really dodged a bullet this time

179
00:09:05,258 --> 00:09:07,771
I always carry money with me for emergencies

180
00:09:07,812 --> 00:09:10,367
Sometimes I put it here, or right over here

181
00:09:11,012 --> 00:09:13,176
Sometimes right here

182
00:09:13,532 --> 00:09:15,533
Or even in here

183
00:09:16,133 --> 00:09:17,574
That's amazing!

184
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:20,149
Let me treat you to a tour of Kyoto this time, okay?

185
00:09:20,216 --> 00:09:22,129
Yay, thank you so much, Hattori-kun!

186
00:09:22,212 --> 00:09:23,345
It really feels like a dream

187
00:09:23,386 --> 00:09:25,170
Oh no, we're in trouble!

188
00:09:25,290 --> 00:09:26,745
What happened?

189
00:09:26,819 --> 00:09:28,081
I see Dad!

190
00:09:31,012 --> 00:09:32,412
Oh no, we're really in trouble this time!

191
00:09:32,604 --> 00:09:34,141
What should we do?

192
00:09:34,182 --> 00:09:36,975
No choice, I'll have to use the Ninja Smoke Screen Technique!

193
00:09:41,173 --> 00:09:42,346
How did this happen? Ouch...

194
00:09:42,387 --> 00:09:43,793
Oh, I'm sorry!

195
00:09:46,844 --> 00:09:47,706
What's going on?

196
00:09:48,073 --> 00:09:49,431
I'm sorry, ouch!

197
00:09:50,837 --> 00:09:52,150
How did this happen?

198
00:09:52,558 --> 00:09:54,200
We've arrived in Kyoto!

199
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:57,172
-Oh, hurry, don't bump into them!
-Hurry...

200
00:09:58,925 --> 00:10:00,084
This is Kinkaku-ji Temple

201
00:10:00,124 --> 00:10:01,872
It's so dazzlingly golden!

202
00:10:03,122 --> 00:10:04,651
This is the Five-Story Pagoda

203
00:10:04,739 --> 00:10:06,082
It looks like a roast chicken!

204
00:10:06,679 --> 00:10:08,082
This is Ryoan-ji Temple

205
00:10:08,321 --> 00:10:09,977
It fills you with awe

206
00:10:10,476 --> 00:10:11,993
This is Kiyomizu-dera Temple

207
00:10:12,034 --> 00:10:13,650
It's so high up?

208
00:10:14,711 --> 00:10:16,340
Hattori-kun, you're the best!

209
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:18,178
-We had so much fun
-Yeah

210
00:10:18,422 --> 00:10:21,268
This is the Movie Studio Park where they film period dramas

211
00:10:21,335 --> 00:10:23,962
So this is the Movie Studio Park, it feels like going back in time!

212
00:10:24,003 --> 00:10:26,421
That's right... You must be big movie stars!

213
00:10:26,708 --> 00:10:28,309
Movie stars? Awesome!

214
00:10:28,392 --> 00:10:30,748
Could you give me an autograph...

215
00:10:30,788 --> 00:10:31,900
Please!

216
00:10:32,303 --> 00:10:34,650
-Luckily, we finally finished all our errands
-Yeah

217
00:10:34,709 --> 00:10:37,748
And we even have time to do some sightseeing, oh!

218
00:10:37,837 --> 00:10:40,880
Why is there a crowd? Could there be a celebrity here?

219
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:42,194
Let's go take a look

220
00:10:47,048 --> 00:10:48,690
Hattori-kun is really getting ahead of himself

221
00:10:48,730 --> 00:10:50,292
Acting like he's a real star

222
00:10:50,332 --> 00:10:52,174
Oh no, it's Dad and Mom!

223
00:10:53,530 --> 00:10:55,283
I have to warn Hattori-kun!

224
00:11:01,179 --> 00:11:02,620
What should we do now?

225
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:04,181
If you're really a ninja hound

226
00:11:04,221 --> 00:11:05,447
You should think of something!

227
00:11:05,488 --> 00:11:06,384
Okay...

228
00:11:18,369 --> 00:11:22,088
-So pretty...
-Oh, it's so beautiful...

229
00:11:23,028 --> 00:11:26,386
That was incredible! I've never seen such beautiful fireworks!

230
00:11:31,468 --> 00:11:33,669
-Shishimaru, you're amazing!
-You flatter me

231
00:11:33,709 --> 00:11:35,949
All right, time's up, we have to head back

232
00:11:35,989 --> 00:11:38,381
Thanks for taking us around Kyoto today

233
00:11:38,521 --> 00:11:39,934
Yan...

234
00:11:46,023 --> 00:11:48,500
I had a wonderful time on this trip too

235
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:49,660
And this time, we even met

236
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:52,458
-A popular movie star!
-I really wanted you to tour Kyoto too

237
00:11:52,499 --> 00:11:55,295
It's fine, just take me along next time!

238
00:11:55,335 --> 00:11:56,061
Yeah

239
00:11:56,102 --> 00:11:57,302
-Ling...
-Right?

240
00:11:57,343 --> 00:11:58,662
Yan...

241
00:11:58,703 --> 00:12:00,851
Regarding the strange incident at Kyoto's Movie Studio Park

242
00:12:00,892 --> 00:12:03,250
our station captured some very precious footage

243
00:12:03,290 --> 00:12:04,609
The fireworks at the time were wonderful

244
00:12:04,650 --> 00:12:06,251
and very rare too

245
00:12:06,292 --> 00:12:07,565
Yan...

246
00:12:08,575 --> 00:12:10,281
Hey, Hattori-kun, what are you doing?

247
00:12:10,502 --> 00:12:12,181
Why aren't you eating the souvenirs we brought back?

248
00:12:12,221 --> 00:12:14,093
They're delicious! Hurry and have some, Hattori-kun

249
00:12:14,301 --> 00:12:16,220
I'll eat them in a little bit

250
00:12:16,268 --> 00:12:17,402
Whew

251
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:20,259
That was a really close shave just now, good thing I covered it

252
00:12:22,706 --> 00:12:25,446
"Lots of Gold Coins"

253
00:12:27,838 --> 00:12:28,940
The newspaper says

254
00:12:29,039 --> 00:12:32,403
60 gold coins were found at a construction site

255
00:12:32,443 --> 00:12:33,845
I'm so jealous

256
00:12:33,885 --> 00:12:35,407
Why don't we go digging around too?

257
00:12:35,447 --> 00:12:37,770
Who knows, maybe we'll make an amazing discovery

258
00:12:38,016 --> 00:12:40,063
Yeah, let's definitely go dig

259
00:12:40,894 --> 00:12:42,095
How could there be anything underground here?

260
00:12:42,136 --> 00:12:44,370
There's never seemed to be anything unusual

261
00:12:44,530 --> 00:12:47,729
Though if we really dug up gold coins, that'd be wonderful

262
00:12:47,770 --> 00:12:49,555
You're totally right, Kenichi

263
00:12:49,596 --> 00:12:51,221
Once we strike it rich, we won't have to work anymore

264
00:12:51,261 --> 00:12:52,622
And I could sleep in in the mornings

265
00:12:52,662 --> 00:12:54,063
Stop daydreaming

266
00:12:54,103 --> 00:12:55,655
Look what time it is now

267
00:12:56,889 --> 00:12:58,875
- Oh no, it really is past the time
- Oh no, I'm late too!

268
00:13:00,567 --> 00:13:01,333
Big brother

269
00:13:01,373 --> 00:13:03,728
Can ancient gold coins actually be used nowadays?

270
00:13:03,768 --> 00:13:05,728
I know that gold coins can't just be used

271
00:13:05,768 --> 00:13:08,899
they're also extremely valuable and popular

272
00:13:09,409 --> 00:13:10,529
Speaking of which

273
00:13:10,569 --> 00:13:12,930
the three of us have been staying at Kenichi's place for so long

274
00:13:12,970 --> 00:13:14,370
I really feel bad

275
00:13:14,410 --> 00:13:17,384
We haven't even paid a single dime for room and board

276
00:13:18,091 --> 00:13:20,191
Then aren't we just freeloading?

277
00:13:20,290 --> 00:13:22,757
I never even thought about it, that was so careless of me

278
00:13:22,798 --> 00:13:25,049
Impacting their finances like this isn't good

279
00:13:25,089 --> 00:13:26,724
It's really not right

280
00:13:31,661 --> 00:13:34,254
You want to pay room and board for two people and a dog?

281
00:13:34,294 --> 00:13:35,893
- Yes, that's right
- It's better this way

282
00:13:35,933 --> 00:13:38,572
Hattori-kun, why would you do that? You're making me angry

283
00:13:38,612 --> 00:13:40,731
I treat you all as kids of the Mitsuba family

284
00:13:40,771 --> 00:13:43,029
We're not so poor that we need to take boarding fees from kids

285
00:13:43,070 --> 00:13:44,445
I won't allow you to do that

286
00:13:44,730 --> 00:13:46,849
Mom's words really touched me

287
00:13:46,889 --> 00:13:48,408
- Yeah
- So touching

288
00:13:48,448 --> 00:13:49,848
Well, even though she says that

289
00:13:49,888 --> 00:13:51,927
we still can't just give nothing, you know

290
00:13:51,967 --> 00:13:53,853
What should I do then?

291
00:13:56,676 --> 00:13:57,620
Yumeko

292
00:13:57,660 --> 00:13:59,165
Did you see today's newspaper?

293
00:13:59,206 --> 00:14:01,934
Yes, wouldn't it be great if we found some gold coins?

294
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:03,582
I'm home!

295
00:14:06,407 --> 00:14:08,646
Shishimaru, why did you give me a piece of paper?

296
00:14:09,018 --> 00:14:11,497
The location is: take three steps back, then dig at your head

297
00:14:11,538 --> 00:14:12,711
What does that mean?

298
00:14:13,764 --> 00:14:15,199
Start from here?

299
00:14:16,729 --> 00:14:18,109
Start from here, right?

300
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:19,043
One, two, three steps

301
00:14:19,083 --> 00:14:20,736
And then dig at the head, right?

302
00:14:20,935 --> 00:14:23,226
Meaning the shadow of the head, that's it...

303
00:14:25,534 --> 00:14:27,389
Woah, it's a gold coin!

304
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:30,733
Mom, I dug up a gold coin!

305
00:14:30,774 --> 00:14:33,178
What? It's a gold coin?

306
00:14:35,178 --> 00:14:37,701
A gold coin! Th-This really is a gold coin!

307
00:14:38,525 --> 00:14:40,755
I dug up the gold coin right here

308
00:14:41,224 --> 00:14:43,305
Mrs. Mitsuba, did something happen?

309
00:14:43,346 --> 00:14:44,004
A gold...

310
00:14:44,044 --> 00:14:45,382
Oh... N-Nothing at all

311
00:14:45,423 --> 00:14:48,392
W-We were just wondering what to make for dinner tonight

312
00:14:48,872 --> 00:14:50,313
Who on earth put it there?

313
00:14:50,353 --> 00:14:51,353
I don't know

314
00:14:51,393 --> 00:14:54,235
When a gold coin is found, it's treated as government property

315
00:14:54,275 --> 00:14:55,643
However, if there is sufficient proof

316
00:14:55,684 --> 00:14:57,516
showing that it belonged to the finder's ancestors

317
00:14:57,557 --> 00:14:58,309
then this gold coin

318
00:14:58,350 --> 00:15:00,277
will belong to the person who found it

319
00:15:00,329 --> 00:15:02,758
What? You even need proof of ancestral treasure?

320
00:15:02,831 --> 00:15:03,918
If there is no proof

321
00:15:03,958 --> 00:15:06,275
the police will hold onto it for a year

322
00:15:06,315 --> 00:15:08,081
before you can claim it

323
00:15:08,193 --> 00:15:10,790
Anyway, any gold coins found must first be turned over to the police

324
00:15:11,122 --> 00:15:13,965
I have no choice, I don't want to lose it so I'll keep it here

325
00:15:14,006 --> 00:15:16,032
- Ouch!
- Yan...

326
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:17,746
Hattori-kun, you were here all along?

327
00:15:17,786 --> 00:15:19,028
You heard everything, didn't you?

328
00:15:19,068 --> 00:15:20,509
It's fine if Hattori-kun knows

329
00:15:20,549 --> 00:15:22,311
Just please don't tell Shinzo

330
00:15:22,351 --> 00:15:24,164
Because he can't keep a secret

331
00:15:24,553 --> 00:15:26,304
What are you saying about me?

332
00:15:27,479 --> 00:15:28,717
Are you guys going to the police station?

333
00:15:28,757 --> 00:15:30,369
Then I'll be your bodyguard

334
00:15:30,609 --> 00:15:32,529
So you heard everything too?

335
00:15:32,769 --> 00:15:35,879
No one will ever know I have a gold coin on me

336
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,266
Yan...

337
00:15:39,681 --> 00:15:40,983
Where did Hattori-kun go?

338
00:15:41,024 --> 00:15:43,922
You're walking so slowly! Big brother is already far ahead

339
00:15:44,124 --> 00:15:46,145
Excuse me, Mr. Police Officer, I'd like to ask you something

340
00:15:46,186 --> 00:15:47,253
Where is that voice coming from?

341
00:15:47,709 --> 00:15:48,990
Who is it? Who's there?

342
00:15:49,801 --> 00:15:51,440
My heart almost stopped!

343
00:15:51,481 --> 00:15:52,799
If someone finds a gold coin

344
00:15:52,839 --> 00:15:54,279
but has no proof it belonged to their ancestors

345
00:15:54,319 --> 00:15:56,476
does that mean they can't keep the coin?

346
00:15:56,517 --> 00:15:58,741
Little boy, did you find a gold coin?

347
00:15:58,782 --> 00:16:01,040
No, I was just wondering

348
00:16:01,596 --> 00:16:03,599
Yes, you're absolutely right

349
00:16:03,639 --> 00:16:05,561
If I give my gold coin to the police now

350
00:16:05,601 --> 00:16:07,684
I'll have to wait a whole year to get it back

351
00:16:07,724 --> 00:16:08,851
No way!

352
00:16:08,937 --> 00:16:09,853
Don't overthink it

353
00:16:09,894 --> 00:16:11,807
Wait until you actually dig up a gold coin first

354
00:16:13,012 --> 00:16:15,175
Hey Kenichi, where are you sneaking off to?

355
00:16:15,215 --> 00:16:16,839
I have something to do

356
00:16:17,006 --> 00:16:18,780
What are you holding in your hand?

357
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,519
Nothing, it's nothing!

358
00:16:20,742 --> 00:16:22,479
You're still trying to hide it from me, aren't you?

359
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,570
There's definitely something fishy going on

360
00:16:23,610 --> 00:16:25,028
- Let me see it!
- No, it's nothing like that!

361
00:16:25,088 --> 00:16:26,817
-Hand it over!
-Hey...

362
00:16:27,394 --> 00:16:28,808
Huh? It's a gold coin...

363
00:16:28,961 --> 00:16:30,044
There are bodyguards here

364
00:16:30,085 --> 00:16:31,324
How outrageous!

365
00:16:31,590 --> 00:16:33,790
-Oh no, trouble!
-Short Boomerang!

366
00:16:34,450 --> 00:16:35,973
Ow, watch out!

367
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:44,020
-Aah, help!
-Run!

368
00:16:44,061 --> 00:16:45,264
You ruined all my cacti!

369
00:16:45,306 --> 00:16:46,189
How outrageous!

370
00:16:46,230 --> 00:16:47,976
-Help!
-How despicable! Hurry and run!

371
00:16:48,087 --> 00:16:49,565
Hurry up and run...

372
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:50,696
Run!

373
00:16:50,909 --> 00:16:52,591
Bodyguard, where is my gold coin?

374
00:16:52,631 --> 00:16:54,352
I don't know who took it either

375
00:16:54,392 --> 00:16:56,114
So you mean someone snatched it?

376
00:16:56,154 --> 00:16:57,934
That's exactly what I mean

377
00:16:58,369 --> 00:16:59,490
I'm home

378
00:16:59,816 --> 00:17:01,014
Where are you guys?

379
00:17:02,865 --> 00:17:05,171
I heard you guys dug up a gold coin, is that true?

380
00:17:05,211 --> 00:17:06,453
Such happy news

381
00:17:06,493 --> 00:17:07,695
We ought to celebrate, right?

382
00:17:07,735 --> 00:17:08,536
It's already gone

383
00:17:08,576 --> 00:17:09,842
We lost it

384
00:17:10,278 --> 00:17:11,685
It's gone? Oh dear

385
00:17:11,725 --> 00:17:13,992
The gold coin is gone? What should we do?

386
00:17:14,138 --> 00:17:15,948
So you had the gold coin, Big Brother?

387
00:17:15,988 --> 00:17:16,990
Yes, that's right

388
00:17:17,031 --> 00:17:19,989
I thought that if I just gave it to Mom, she definitely wouldn't accept it

389
00:17:20,029 --> 00:17:21,748
So I used that method

390
00:17:21,788 --> 00:17:24,453
Who knew we'd have to leave it at the police station for a whole year before getting it back

391
00:17:24,494 --> 00:17:25,734
Then what should we do?

392
00:17:26,068 --> 00:17:28,188
But I know another way

393
00:17:28,228 --> 00:17:31,028
If we have a certificate from our ancestors, that'll do it

394
00:17:31,068 --> 00:17:32,113
Here, watch this

395
00:17:32,154 --> 00:17:35,189
This is document forgery, a ninja art!

396
00:17:36,298 --> 00:17:38,185
Eek, a mouse!

397
00:17:38,226 --> 00:17:40,695
Oh, I wonder what that mouse left behind?

398
00:17:41,144 --> 00:17:42,303
Turns out it's a piece of paper?

399
00:17:42,343 --> 00:17:43,583
Oh, it's a gold coin!

400
00:17:43,623 --> 00:17:45,072
-What? A gold coin?
-A gold coin?

401
00:17:45,529 --> 00:17:46,941
There really is a gold coin here!

402
00:17:46,981 --> 00:17:47,863
Mom, take a look

403
00:17:47,904 --> 00:17:49,333
"This is a certificate from our ancestors"

404
00:17:49,374 --> 00:17:51,098
"This gold coin is a gift for our grandson Kenichi"

405
00:17:51,139 --> 00:17:52,915
-That's amazing, a gold coin!
-Hooray...

406
00:17:52,956 --> 00:17:53,950
That's strange, though

407
00:17:53,991 --> 00:17:56,910
How would our ancestors have known
Kenichi's name?

408
00:17:57,352 --> 00:17:58,383
That's true

409
00:17:58,424 --> 00:18:00,915
Could this be an idea Hattori-kun came up with?

410
00:18:01,188 --> 00:18:02,350
Now that I think about it, it seems likely

411
00:18:02,390 --> 00:18:04,272
Hattori-kun, where are you?

412
00:18:04,312 --> 00:18:05,634
Come out right now!

413
00:18:05,674 --> 00:18:06,460
Now we're in trouble

414
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,638
I carelessly wrote the name "Kenichi"

415
00:18:08,678 --> 00:18:10,259
I really overdid it

416
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,907
Let's get out of here quickly

417
00:18:13,430 --> 00:18:15,580
Oh well, everybody knows that sometimes

418
00:18:15,620 --> 00:18:17,254
Things just don't go so smoothly

419
00:18:17,295 --> 00:18:18,362
Yan...
